<p>
	It is a joy to welcome you into our program! Please take some time to read through this
	handbook so you understand our expectations for our time together. A hard copy also lives in
	the policy notebook on the parent counter, along with more detailed information on certain
	topics.
</p>
	<p>
		As always, if you have any questions or concerns, please let us know — we would love
		to talk with you more about our policies and procedures.
	</p>

<h2>Mission</h2>
<p>
	At Wild Pear, our goal is to meet children where they are at developmentally and encourage
	them to move forward in their own unique way. With an emphasis on social and emotional
	health and grounded in a foundation of connected relationships, we engage in activities that
	invite children to practice a wide range of skill building. Providing time away from a busy
	fast-paced life, we offer space and time for holistic, multifaceted education inspired by direct
	experiences with food, gardens, and nature.
</p>

<h2>Inclusion and Anti-Bias Policy</h2>
<p>
	Wild Pear Preschool is an inclusive and welcoming school, meaning your family will be accepted
	and valued here. We will see and honor you and your child's race, religion, gender, ability,
	orientation, class, country of origin, immigration status, language, and education level. We
	respect all family structures; whether you are connected by blood, or law, or love alone, you
	are welcome here.
</p>
<p>
	We actively teach anti-bias curriculum at WPP, presented and discussed in an age-appropriate
	and relevant manner. Anti-bias work, like most work with young children, is ongoing, ever
	growing, and requires intentional self-work on the part of the adults entrusted to teach them. If
	you ever feel that a part of your or your child's identity is being disrespected, ignored, or
	uncelebrated, please bring it to our attention and we will find a way to correct it.
</p>

<h2>Hours, Calendar, and Closures</h2>
<p>
	We are open Monday through Friday, 7:30am until 5:30pm. Our school year begins in September
	and runs until mid-June. We reopen at the end of June to welcome the children back for summer camp!
</p>
<p>
	Our full calendar — including staff meeting early closures, family conferences,
	holidays, and seasonal breaks — is shared with enrolled families and posted in the policy
	notebook. 
</p>
	<p>
		A few highlights: the school year begins September 4th, 2025, we close for Fall
		Break (Nov 27-28), Winter Break (Dec 22-Jan 2), Spring Break (Mar 23-27), and the last day of
		the school year is June 12th, 2026.
	</p>

<AlertWarning title="Winter Weather">
	We love having children at school on snowy days and will gear up and play outside as long as
	it's safe to do so. If roads are dangerously icy in the morning we may have a delayed start; if a
	winter storm presents a likely risk of power outages or falling trees, we will be closed.
</AlertWarning>
<p>
	We understand that for many families, preschool is critical child care, not just an enrichment
	activity. In the rare case of an unscheduled closure we will notify you as soon as possible, but it
	is your responsibility to arrange for back-up care in the event we need to close unexpectedly.
</p>

