<h2>Wild Pear Campus</h2>
<p>
	You're welcome to park in our small lot, in the two side-by-side driveways, on our side of the
	street, or in the church parking lot. We have three large fenced play yards on campus: the
	"Lower Yard" beside the blue house, the "Sprouts Yard" directly behind the white house, and the
	"School Age Yard" behind the Sprouts Yard near the teal garage.
</p>
<p>
	Please help us protect the plants and wildlife on the property by staying on the graveled,
	bark-chipped, or paved paths outside the designated play yards, and help us teach children that
	"gates are for grown-ups," making sure all gates are closed securely behind you. For everyone's
	safety, children under age 5 are never permitted to move around campus without an adult
	directly accompanying them, including going between sites or to the bathroom — and please
	never leave a child under 5 alone in a car, even briefly.
</p>

<h2>Arrival and Departure</h2>
<p>
	Most days, children are dropped off outside in their play yard, where you'll sign them in using
	our app. Before you leave, make sure your child is set for the weather, and that a teacher knows
	you are passing off your child. If your child needs extra support during separation, please plan
	to arrive before 8:15 — once the school day starts, teachers need to shift their attention to
	breakfast and circle time. Children may not arrive after 8:30 without a prior arrangement or a
	true emergency.
</p>
<p>
	If your child has a hard time separating, that's completely typical! You're welcome to stay for a
	few minutes and play, invite your child to wave through the fence, let them hold a family photo,
	or ask a teacher to hold your child's hand while you leave. We find it's best to give your child a
	clear, confident goodbye rather than lingering, which can be confusing for both children and
	teachers.
</p>
<p>
	At pickup, you'll sign your child out using the app and make sure a teacher knows you're leaving
	together. Children are only released to custodial parents or legal guardians unless you've
	specified otherwise on your enrollment forms; anyone unfamiliar to the teacher may be asked to
	show ID. We ask that visiting time at pickup be kept to about 10 minutes, and that any concerns
	about another child be brought to a teacher rather than handled directly, out of respect for that
	family's privacy and our supervision responsibilities. Please don't take photos or videos while
	you're here, since many children have specific photo-release plans in place. If your child is not
	picked up on time, a $1.00-per-minute late fee applies past 5:30pm, based on the teacher's
	clock.
</p>

